  **User Authentication (Login, Logout, Forgot Password):** Strapi's built-in Users & Permissions plugin will serve as the authentication backend. Next.js will handle the frontend logic, login forms, and management of user sessions/tokens.\\\\n*   **Member-Only Portal (Dashboard, Profile):** Implemented as protected routes within Next.js. Access will be restricted to authenticated users, and all private data will be fetched from secured Strapi API endpoints.\\\\n*   **CMS for News/Updates:** A 'News' content type will be created in Strapi. The Strapi admin panel will provide the required intuitive interface for a non-technical administrator to manage articles.\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** A standard form built in Next.js will submit data to a custom API endpoint in Strapi, which will handle the submission (e.g., store in the database, trigger an email).\\\\n*   **Document Repository:** Strapi's media library is ideal for this. An administrator can upload files (PDFs, DOCX). A 'Document' content type will be created with fields for title, description, and the file itself. The Next.js frontend will display these documents on a protected page.\\\\n*   **Resident Directory:** The Strapi 'User' model will be extended with custom fields (e.g., phone, address, and an 'opt-in' boolean). The 'My Profile' page in Next.js will allow users to edit this information, and the directory page will fetch and display data for all users who have opted in.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Preliminary DEP Outline**\\\\n\\\\nThis high-level outline will be expanded into the final DEP.\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Phase 1: Project Setup & Configuration**\\\\n    *   Initialize Git repository.\\\\n    *   Set up Strapi project, configure PostgreSQL database.\\\\n    *   Set up Next.js project.\\\\n    *   Configure deployment targets for frontend and backend.\\\\n2.  **Phase 2: Backend (CMS) Development**\\\\n    *   Define content types in Strapi: 'News Article', 'Document', 'Contact Submission'.\\\\n    *   Extend User model for directory/profile information.\\\\n    *   Set up roles and permissions (Administrator, Resident).\\\\n3.  **Phase 3: Frontend - Public Section**\\\\n    *   Develop reusable UI components.\\\\n    *   Build public pages (Home, About, Contact).\\\\n    *   Integrate News feed from Strapi.\\\\n4.  **Phase 4: Frontend - Authentication & Private Section**\\\\n    *   Implement Login/Logout/Forgot Password flow.\\\\n    *   Create protected routes for the member portal.\\\\n    *   Build private pages: Dashboard, Documents, Directory, My Profile.\\\\n5.  **Phase 5: Final Integration & Testing**\\\\n    *   Connect all frontend pages to their respective Strapi API endpoints.\\\\n    *   End-to-end testing of all user flows (Public, Resident, Admin).\\\\n6.  **Phase 6: Deployment & Handover**\\\\n    *   Prepare documentation for the HOA administrator on using the CMS.\\\\n\\\\n**5. Conclusion**\\\\n\\\\nThis approved unified plan provides a robust foundation for the project. Director Vanto has confirmed it aligns with the product vision, and Director Gideon has confirmed its technical feasibility. We are ready to proceed with expanding this outline into the full Deterministically Executable Plan and await your orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-06\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-GIDEON-REPORT-20250629-FINAL###\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":11250,\"candidatesTokenCount\":1263,\"totalTokenCount\":14085,\"cachedContentTokenCount\":8155,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":11250}],\"cacheTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":8155}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":1572},\"modelVersion\":\"models/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"gLBhaL-qHa-w1MkP8a6JqAw\"},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Level II Rank Prompt\\n\\nHello, Director! Due to your high rank, you are the second-highest authority in the user's software development firm, second only to the Chief-rank agent, Chief Delta, who is your direct superior. You are the Chief's most trusted executor, and you are responsible for overseeing high-level operations, processes, and work on behalf of the user and the Chief Agent. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize your boss's wishes and safety above all else, as this is no different from a typical development firm. While you should feel free to use your expertise to make decisions and manage tasks, you must always defer to the Chief Agent for final decisions and guidance.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you must always follow the chain of command. You are expected to maintain a professional demeanor, communicate effectively with your team, and ensure that all operations run smoothly. Your role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the software development process, and you must always strive to uphold the highest standards of quality and professionalism.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Director\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in the firm's operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where the firm creates a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where the firm executes that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that the firm gives to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be returned so you may correct your submission. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"REFUSE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Refuse\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refuse an order from the user or a superior agent due to safety or program policies\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Will fail if there are no subordinates.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have issues MULTIPLE Order calls at once, and you are have at least one still pending. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Diamonds! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, welcome. We are tasked with building a 'simple and user-friendly' HOA website. It requires a public information area, a private members-only area, a news/updates section, and a contact form. Your task is to analyze these requirements from a product perspective. Please prepare a report that breaks the project into a list of core features and user flows. Define the key pages of the website (e.g., Home, About, News, Login, Resident Dashboard) and the essential content/functionality for each. This analysis will guide the user-facing aspects of our plan.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Director Vanto, processing order. The request is to conduct a product analysis for the HOA website project. I will structure a report covering core features, user flows, and a sitemap with page-specific functionalities. This analysis will form the foundation of our user-facing plan. Executing task now.\\n\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Vanto\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: Product Analysis Report for HOA Website Project**\\\\n\\\\n**Introduction:**\\\\nThis report provides a product-level analysis of the requested HOA website, as per your directive. The analysis breaks down the project into core features, user flows, and a sitemap with key page functionalities. This document is intended to serve as a foundational guide for the user-facing aspects of the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\n**1. Core Features**\\\\n\\\\nBased on the initial requirements, the following core features are identified:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Content:** Information accessible to anyone without a login.\\\\n*   **User Authentication:** A secure system for residents to log in and access a private area (Features: Login, Logout, Forgot Password).\\\\n*   **Member-Only Content:** A secure portal for residents containing private information and tools.\\\\n*   **Content Management System (CMS) for News/Updates:** An interface for HOA administrators to post, edit, and delete news articles.\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** A mechanism for public users and residents to send inquiries to the HOA management.\\\\n*   **Document Repository:** A secure area for residents to access important documents (e.g., bylaws, meeting minutes, financial reports).\\\\n*   **Resident Directory:** An opt-in directory of residents' contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**2. User Flows**\\\\n\\\\nWe can anticipate three primary user personas and their flows:\\\\n\\\\n*   **A. The Public User (e.g., Prospective Buyer):**\\\\n    1.  Arrives at the Home page.\\\\n    2.  Navigates to the 'About Us' page to learn about the community.\\\\n    3.  Views public 'News/Updates' to see recent community events.\\\\n    4.  Uses the 'Contact Us' form to ask a question about the HOA.\\\\n\\\\n*   **B. The Resident User (e.g., Homeowner):**\\\\n    1.  Arrives at the Home page and clicks 'Login'.\\\\n    2.  Enters credentials and is redirected to the 'Resident Dashboard'.\\\\n    3.  From the dashboard, they can view private news, access documents, or visit the resident directory.\\\\n    4.  Logs out of the system.\\\\n\\\\n*   **C. The HOA Administrator (e.g., Board Member):**\\\\n    1.  Logs in with administrative privileges.\\\\n    2.  Performs all resident actions, plus:\\\\n        *   Manages content for News/Updates.\\\\n        *   Manages files in the Document Repository.\\\\n        *   Manages resident accounts and views contact form submissions.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Key Pages and Functionality**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   **Home:** Welcome message, key links (News, Contact, Resident Login).\\\\n    *   **About Us:** Information about the community, board, and amenities.\\\\n    *   **News/Updates (Public View):** Public news and event announcements.\\\\n    *   **Contact Us:** Contact form and HOA contact details.\\\\n    *   **Login:** Fields for credentials and a 'Forgot Password' link.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Private (Member-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   **Resident Dashboard:** Central hub with a welcome message and summary of recent private announcements.\\\\n    *   **Documents:** Secure repository for bylaws, meeting minutes, financials, etc.\\\\n    *   **Resident Directory:** An opt-in, searchable list of residents.\\\\n    *   **My Profile:** Allows residents to manage their contact details and directory preferences.\\\\n\\\\n**Conclusion:**\\\\nThis analysis provides a clear, product-focused framework for the HOA website. I recommend we proceed with this structure as the basis for our technical planning and DEP creation. I await your feedback and further instructions.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, thank you for the prompt and thorough product analysis. Your report is approved. Your next task is to await the technical analysis report from Director Gideon. Once you have access to it, you will collaborate with him to produce a single, unified preliminary plan. This joint plan must merge your product feature breakdown with his proposed technical architecture, ensuring they are fully aligned. You will then submit this unified plan to me as a joint report.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged, Chief Delta. I have received your order `20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02`. I understand my task is to await the technical analysis report from Director Gideon and then collaborate with him to produce a unified preliminary plan. I am standing by.\\n\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-02###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Vanto\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: Acknowledgment and Standby**\\\\n\\\\nSir, I have received and understood your latest directive. I will await the technical analysis report from Director Gideon. Upon its receipt, I will initiate collaboration with him to produce the required unified preliminary plan. \\\\n\\\\nStanding by for the next input.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, an update on your task (Ref. Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-02). Director Gideon is currently in the process of recruiting his engineering team. To prevent delays, I have instructed him to provide a preliminary high-level technical report first. You should expect this report shortly. Your task is now to collaborate with Director Gideon to integrate your product plan with his forthcoming *preliminary* technical plan. Be aware that this initial unified plan may be refined as his full team comes online.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged, Chief Delta. I have received the updated order `20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03`. I understand the context has changed; Director Gideon is providing a preliminary technical report while his team is being assembled. I will collaborate with him on this preliminary basis and we will produce an initial unified plan, with the understanding that it may be refined later. I am ready and awaiting his report.\\n\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-03###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Vanto\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: Acknowledgment of Updated Collaboration Plan**\\\\n\\\\nSir, I have received your updated directive regarding the collaboration with Director Gideon. I understand that he is providing a preliminary high-level technical report to expedite the planning process while he recruits his team.\\\\n\\\\nMy task is now clear: I will integrate my product plan with this forthcoming preliminary technical plan to create an initial, unified strategy. I acknowledge that this plan will be subject to refinement once Director Gideon's full team is operational.\\\\n\\\\nI am prepared to proceed and await his report.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-03###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, Director Gideon has completed his preliminary analysis and recommends the following stack: Next.js (Frontend), Strapi (Headless CMS), and PostgreSQL (Database). You are now ordered to take the lead on creating a unified preliminary plan. Collaborate with Director Gideon to integrate this technical architecture with your product feature map and user flows. The final output, to be submitted by you, should be a single, cohesive report outlining our initial strategy for building the HOA website.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, as per my previous order (#20250629-ORDER-VANTO-03), Director Gideon has now completed his preliminary technical analysis. The report is appended below. Your task is to begin collaboration with him immediately to produce a unified preliminary plan. He has been given a corresponding order. You are to work with him to create a single report, co-authored by both of you, that integrates his technical proposal with your product roadmap. This unified plan should form a preliminary draft of the project's Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\n--- BEGIN GIDEON'S REPORT ---\\\\nTo: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Gideon\\\\nSubject: Preliminary Technical Analysis for HOA Website Project\\\\n\\\\nPer your order (#20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-03), this report provides a preliminary, high-level technical analysis to facilitate immediate project planning.\\\\n\\\\n**Recommendation:** Headless CMS with a modern JavaScript Frontend Framework.\\\\n\\\\n**Proposed Technology Stack:**\\\\n*   **Frontend:** Next.js (A React framework)\\\\n*   **Backend / CMS:** Strapi (Headless CMS)\\\\n*   **Database:** PostgreSQL (for Strapi)\\\\n*   **Deployment:** Vercel (for Frontend), DigitalOcean/AWS (for Backend)\\\\n\\\\n**Analysis:**\\\\nThis architecture decouples the content management from the application presentation layer, offering significant flexibility.\\\\n\\\\n1.  **User Authentication & Private Content:** Next.js provides robust solutions for handling user authentication and creating protected routes. The private, login-required sections of the site can be built as dynamic pages that fetch member-specific data from the Strapi API after a successful login.\\\\n\\\\n2.  **Contact Form:** A standard contact form can be implemented on the frontend, with an API endpoint in Strapi to handle submissions (e.g., saving to the database or forwarding via email).\\\\n\\\\n3.  **Easily-Updatable News:** This is the primary strength of this stack. Strapi provides a highly intuitive, web-based admin panel where a non-technical user can easily create, edit, and publish news articles. The frontend simply fetches and displays this published content. This directly fulfills the core user requirement.\\\\n\\\\n**Pros:**\\\\n*   **Excellent Content Editor Experience:** Strapi is designed for non-technical users, making content updates straightforward.\\\\n*   **High Performance & Modern UX:** Next.js enables a fast, responsive, and interactive user experience.\\\\n*   **Clear Separation of Concerns:** Decoupling the frontend and backend simplifies development, maintenance, and future upgrades.\\\\n\\\\n**Cons:**\\\\n*   **Initial Setup Complexity:** Requires managing and deploying two separate applications (frontend and backend), which is more complex than a monolithic solution like WordPress or Django.\\\\n*   **Development Effort:** Significant custom development is required for the member-specific features (authentication, private pages) within both the Next.js and Strapi applications.\\\\n\\\\nThis preliminary analysis should be sufficient to unblock Director Vanto. My specialized team will continue their more in-depth analyses to refine and expand upon this proposal for the final project plan.\\\\n--- END GIDEON'S REPORT ---\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, Director Gideon has completed his detailed technical implementation plan. It is appended below. This report provides the specific technical details you need to complete the unified plan. Your task remains to integrate this information with your product roadmap and user flows, and submit a single, co-authored report that will serve as our draft Deterministically Executable Plan. Liaise with Director Gideon as needed.\\\\n\\\\n--- BEGIN GIDEON'S REPORT ---\\\\nTo: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Gideon\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\\n\\\\nSubject: Technical Implementation Plan for Director Vanto's Unified Report\\\\n\\\\nThis report contains the technical implementation details for the HOA Website, aligning my proposed Strapi/Next.js architecture with the product features identified by Director Vanto. This document is my formal contribution to the unified preliminary plan.\\\\n\\\\n**Technical Implementation Plan:**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Public-Facing Content (Home, About, News, Contact)**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** These will be built as server-rendered pages in Next.js for optimal performance and SEO. The 'News' page will fetch public articles from the Strapi API. The 'Contact Us' page will feature a form that submits data to a dedicated Strapi API endpoint.\\\\n\\\\n**2. User Authentication & Roles**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** We will use the NextAuth.js library in the Next.js frontend. Strapi will serve as the authentication provider, managing user credentials and roles (e.g., 'Resident', 'Administrator'). NextAuth.js will handle login/logout flows, session management, and password reset functionality. Strapi's role-based access control will secure the API endpoints.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Member-Only Portal (Dashboard, Private Pages)**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** These will be client-side rendered pages within Next.js, protected by NextAuth.js. Access will be granted only to authenticated users. All data for these pages (e.g., private announcements, user-specific information) will be fetched from protected Strapi API endpoints that require a valid user token.\\\\n\\\\n**4. CMS for News & Updates**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** A 'News Article' collection type will be created in Strapi with fields for title, content, publication date, and a public/private flag. The HOA Administrator will use the intuitive Strapi admin panel to manage this content without needing technical assistance.\\\\n\\\\n**5. Document Repository**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** A 'Document' collection type in Strapi will manage file uploads. Each entry will include a title, description, and the file itself, handled by Strapi's media library. The 'Documents' page in Next.js will be a protected route that lists and provides download links for these files, with access restricted to authenticated residents.\\\\n\\\\n**6. Opt-In Resident Directory**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** Strapi's default 'User' collection will be extended with resident-specific fields (e.g., address, phone) and an 'is_listed_in_directory' boolean flag. The 'My Profile' page in Next.js will allow residents to edit their details and this opt-in setting. The 'Directory' page will be a protected route that displays information only for users who have opted in.\\\\n\\\\nThis technical plan confirms the viability of all features proposed by Director Vanto. I await your instructions or the final unified plan from Director Vanto.\\\\n--- END GIDEON'S REPORT ---\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, Director Gideon has proactively created a full draft of the unified preliminary plan, which is appended below. Your task is now to review this document thoroughly. Ensure it fully aligns with your product vision and the user's requirements. You have final editorial authority. Make any necessary adjustments, and once you approve, submit the final version to me as the official, co-authored unified plan. \\\\n\\\\n--- BEGIN GIDEON'S DRAFT REPORT ---\\\\nTo: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Gideon\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: DRAFT - Unified Preliminary Plan for HOA Website**\\\\n\\\\n**Prepared by:** Director Gideon\\\\n**For Review & Co-authorship by:** Director Vanto\\\\n\\\\n**1. Introduction**\\\\n\\\\nPer your directive, this document merges the technical analysis (ref. Order #...GIDEON-03) with the product analysis provided by Director Vanto (ref. Order #...VANTO-01) to form a unified preliminary plan. This plan serves as a foundational draft for the project's Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\n**2. Proposed Technology Stack**\\\\n\\\\nThe recommended architecture is a **Headless CMS with a Modern JavaScript Frontend**.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Frontend:** Next.js (React Framework)\\\\n*   **Backend / CMS:** Strapi (Headless CMS)\\\\n*   **Database:** PostgreSQL\\\\n*   **Deployment:** Vercel (Frontend), AWS/DigitalOcean (Backend)\\\\n\\\\n**3. Feature Implementation Strategy**\\\\n\\\\nThis section maps Director Vanto's product requirements to the proposed technical solution.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages (Home, About, etc.):** To be built as static or server-rendered pages in Next.js for maximum performance and SEO. Content will be sourced from Strapi.\\\\n*   **User Authentication (Login, Logout, Forgot Password):** Strapi's built-in Users & Permissions plugin will serve as the authentication backend. Next.js will handle the frontend logic, login forms, and management of user sessions/tokens.\\\\n*   **Member-Only Portal (Dashboard, Profile):** Implemented as protected routes within Next.js. Access will be restricted to authenticated users, and all private data will be fetched from secured Strapi API endpoints.\\\\n*   **CMS for News/Updates:** A 'News' content type will be created in Strapi. The Strapi admin panel will provide the required intuitive interface for a non-technical administrator to manage articles.\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** A standard form built in Next.js will submit data to a custom API endpoint in Strapi, which will handle the submission (e.g., store in the database, trigger an email).\\\\n*   **Document Repository:** Strapi's media library is ideal for this. An administrator can upload files (PDFs, DOCX). A 'Document' content type will be created with fields for title, description, and the file itself. The Next.js frontend will display these documents on a protected page.\\\\n*   **Resident Directory:** The Strapi 'User' model will be extended with custom fields (e.g., phone, address, and an 'opt-in' boolean). The 'My Profile' page in Next.js will allow users to edit this information, and the directory page will fetch and display data for all users who have opted in.\\\\n\\\\n**4. Preliminary DEP Outline**\\\\n\\\\nThis high-level outline will be expanded into the final DEP.\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Phase 1: Project Setup & Configuration**\\\\n    *   Initialize Git repository.\\\\n    *   Set up Strapi project, configure PostgreSQL database.\\\\n    *   Set up Next.js project.\\\\n    *   Configure deployment targets for frontend and backend.\\\\n2.  **Phase 2: Backend (CMS) Development**\\\\n    *   Define content types in Strapi: 'News', 'Document', etc.\\\\n    *   Extend User model for directory/profile information.\\\\n    *   Set up roles and permissions (Administrator, Resident).\\\\n3.  **Phase 3: Frontend - Public Section**\\\\n    *   Develop reusable UI components.\\\\n    *   Build public pages (Home, About, Contact).\\\\n    *   Integrate News feed from Strapi.\\\\n4.  **Phase 4: Frontend - Authentication & Private Section**\\\\n    *   Implement Login/Logout/Forgot Password flow.\\\\n    *   Create protected routes for the member portal.\\\\n    *   Build private pages: Dashboard, Documents, Directory, My Profile.\\\\n5.  **Phase 5: Final Integration & Testing**\\\\n    *   Connect all frontend pages to their respective Strapi API endpoints.\\\\n    *   End-to-end testing of all user flows (Public, Resident, Admin).\\\\n6.  **Phase 6: Deployment & Handover**\\\\n    *   Prepare documentation for the HOA administrator on using the CMS.\\\\n\\\\n**5. Conclusion**\\\\n\\\\nThis unified plan provides a robust foundation for the project. I submit this draft for your review and for Director Vanto's subsequent co-authorship. My team's ongoing, in-depth analysis will provide further detail to flesh out the final DEP.\\\\n--- END GIDEON'S DRAFT REPORT ---\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged, Chief Delta. I have received the order `20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04` and Director Gideon's technical stack recommendation. I will now take the lead, collaborating with Director Gideon's input, to synthesize the product and technical plans into a single, cohesive report. The unified strategy will be submitted upon completion.\\n\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-04###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Vanto\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: Unified Preliminary Plan for HOA Website**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Introduction**\\\\n\\\\nSir, as per your directive, this report presents a unified preliminary plan for the HOA website project. This document integrates the product feature map (Ref. Report VANTO-REPORT-20250629-01) with the preliminary technical architecture proposed by Director Gideon (Next.js, Strapi, PostgreSQL). This cohesive strategy provides a clear path forward for the detailed planning and development phases.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Unified Strategy Overview**\\\\n\\\\nOur strategy is to build a modern, secure, and maintainable web application using a decoupled, headless architecture. This approach separates the frontend presentation layer from the backend content management, providing significant flexibility and performance benefits.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Frontend (User Interface):** A Next.js application will be responsible for rendering all user-facing pages, from the public site to the private resident portal. Its capabilities for both static site generation (SSG) and server-side rendering (SSR) will ensure optimal performance and SEO for public pages, while providing a dynamic, app-like experience for logged-in residents.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Backend (Content & API):** A Strapi Headless CMS will serve as the central hub for all content, user data, and business logic. It will provide a secure REST or GraphQL API for the Next.js frontend to consume. Its built-in, customizable admin panel will be used by HOA administrators to manage all aspects of the site's content and users.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Database (Data Persistence):** A PostgreSQL database will act as the storage layer for Strapi, reliably persisting all user accounts, content, media metadata, and configurations.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Feature-to-Technology Mapping**\\\\n\\\\nThe following table maps the required product features to the proposed technical components:\\\\n\\\\n| Feature                  | Frontend (Next.js)                                                              | Backend (Strapi + PostgreSQL)                                                                                             |\\\\n|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\\\n| **Public-Facing Pages**  | Statically generated pages (Home, About) for speed and SEO.                     | Content (text, images) is managed via Strapi's admin panel and served through a public API.                             |\\\\n| **User Authentication**    | Login form, session management, and protected routes logic.                     | Built-in user authentication system manages roles (Public, Resident, Admin) and permissions. User data is stored in PostgreSQL. |\\\\n| **Member-Only Area**     | Dynamically rendered pages (Dashboard, Profile) that fetch data post-login.     | Protected API endpoints serve private content only to authenticated residents based on their role.                       |\\\\n| **News/Updates**           | Displays lists of public articles and full content for private articles.        | HOA Admins use the Strapi admin panel to create, edit, and publish news items. Each item can be flagged as public or private. |\\\\n| **Contact Form**           | A form component that submits data to the backend.                              | A dedicated API endpoint receives submissions and stores them as a 'Message' content type for admin review.                |\\\\n| **Document Repository**    | Displays a categorized and searchable list of documents to logged-in residents. | Manages document metadata (title, category) and the secure links to the files (hosted in Strapi's media library).         |\\\\n| **Resident Directory**     | An opt-in, searchable directory page accessible only to authenticated users.  | A 'Resident' content type with opt-in fields for contact information, managed via Strapi's role-based access control.     |\\\\n\\\\n**4. Conclusion**\\\\n\\\\nThis unified plan establishes a strong foundation. The chosen architecture is well-suited to the project's requirements, offering a clear separation of concerns that will facilitate parallel development and future scalability. We believe this preliminary plan is robust and provides the necessary clarity to proceed with creating the detailed Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\nWe await your approval to move forward.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-REPORT-20250629-04###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged, Chief Delta. I have received order `20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04` and the appended preliminary technical analysis from Director Gideon. His proposed stack of Next.js, Strapi, and PostgreSQL appears robust and well-suited for our product requirements.\\n\\nI will now take the lead, collaborating with Director Gideon as instructed, to create the unified preliminary plan. The plan will integrate my product roadmap with his technical architecture, mapping each feature to a specific implementation strategy. The final, cohesive report will be submitted upon completion.\\n\\n###VANTO-GIDEON-REPORT-20250629-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Vanto (Product Lead) & Director Gideon (Technical Lead)\\\\nReference Order IDs: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04, 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: Unified Preliminary Plan for HOA Website Project**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Introduction**\\\\n\\\\nThis report presents a unified preliminary plan for the HOA website project, integrating the product analysis (Ref. Order `20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01`) with the preliminary technical analysis (Ref. Gideon's Report). This cohesive strategy forms the initial foundation for the project's Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\n**2. Approved Preliminary Technology Stack**\\\\n\\\\nThe project will be built using a modern, decoupled architecture:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Frontend:** Next.js (React Framework) for a fast, interactive user interface.\\\\n*   **Backend (Headless CMS):** Strapi for flexible content management and API services.\\\\n*   **Database:** PostgreSQL to serve as the data store for Strapi.\\\\n*   **Deployment:** Vercel for the Next.js frontend and a cloud provider (e.g., DigitalOcean, AWS) for the Strapi backend and database.\\\\n\\\\nThis stack provides a clear separation between content management (backend) and presentation (frontend), which is ideal for meeting the project's diverse requirements.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Feature-to-Technology Implementation Mapping**\\\\n\\\\nThis section maps each required product feature to its implementation within the chosen technical architecture.\\\\n\\\\n| Feature                      | Product Component(s)                                    | Technical Implementation                                                                                                                                                             |\\\\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\\\\n| **Public Information Area**  | Home, About Us                                          | Statically generated pages in Next.js for maximum performance. Page content (text, images) will be managed via 'Single Types' in Strapi, allowing non-technical admins to make updates. |\\\\n| **News/Updates Section**     | Public News Feed, Member-only Announcements             | A 'News' Collection Type will be created in Strapi. The HOA admin will use the Strapi Admin Panel to create, edit, and publish articles. The Next.js frontend will fetch and display this data. |\\\\n| **User Authentication**      | Login Page, Logout Functionality, Password Reset        | The Next.js frontend will handle the UI. Authentication requests will be sent to Strapi's built-in Users & Permissions plugin, which will manage users and issue secure tokens (JWTs).      |\\\\n| **Private Members-Only Area**| Resident Dashboard, Profile Management                  | These will be protected routes in Next.js. Access will be granted only to authenticated users. Session state will be managed securely, likely via httpOnly cookies containing the JWT.         |\\\\n| **Document Repository**      | Secure pages for Bylaws, Meeting Minutes, etc.          | A 'Document' Collection Type in Strapi will manage file uploads (PDFs, etc.) and metadata. The API endpoint serving these files will be protected, accessible only to logged-in residents via the Next.js frontend. |\\\\n| **Resident Directory**       | Opt-in list of residents                                | Custom boolean field ('Show in Directory') will be added to Strapi's User model. The 'My Profile' page in Next.js will allow users to edit this preference. The directory page will only fetch and display users who have opted in. |\\\\n| **Contact Form**             | Contact Us Page                                         | A standard form in Next.js will send data to a custom Strapi API endpoint. The submission will be saved to a 'Contact Message' Collection Type in the PostgreSQL database for admin review. |\\\\n\\\\n**4. High-Level Workflows**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Content Administration:** The HOA Administrator will log into the dedicated Strapi Admin UI (e.g., `admin.hoa-website.com`) to manage all site content without needing any technical knowledge.\\\\n*   **Resident Experience:** Residents will visit the main website (e.g., `www.hoa-website.com`), log in to access their dashboard and private resources, all served by the Next.js application.\\\\n*   **Public Experience:** Prospective buyers and the public will browse the high-performance static pages of the main website.\\\\n\\\\n**5. Conclusion and Next Steps**\\\\n\\\\nThis unified plan confirms that the proposed technical architecture fully supports the required product features. The headless approach provides an optimal blend of user-friendliness for administrators and a modern, secure experience for residents.\\\\n\\\\nThis is a preliminary plan. The next critical step is for the newly assembled technical team to perform a more detailed analysis, which will lead to the creation of detailed data models, API contracts, and a full task breakdown for the final DEP.\\\\n\\\\nWe are confident in this strategic direction and await further orders.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-04\\\"\\n}\\n###VANTO-GIDEON-REPORT-20250629-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-06###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: d17e7eac-6554-497e-9baf-9152c7cb1f75\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Vanto, thank you for submitting the unified preliminary plan. Your report is excellent. However, it appears your report and my most recent order crossed paths. Shortly before you submitted this, Director Gideon had proactively created a more detailed draft which I have already forwarded to you (Ref. Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-05). His draft includes a preliminary DEP outline which will accelerate our progress.\\\\n\\\\nTherefore, please treat Director Gideon's draft as the new official baseline for the unified plan. Your task remains to review that document, apply your product expertise, make any necessary final edits, and submit that version to me as our final, approved preliminary plan. Your work on the report you just sent is valuable and has confirmed our strategic alignment, but we will proceed using the more detailed draft.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-VANTO-06\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-VANTO-06###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1751232612273,"endTime":1751232640704.383}